  "ground_truth_reference": {
    "note": "Ground truth is IDENTICAL across all four models in this yolo-native-test harness (same frozen data/yolo/test manifest, built independently of the contaminated data/detector rebuilt_split_manifest.csv used for the earlier/exploratory evaluation). A copy of ground_truth_yolo_native_test_coco.json is included in this folder for self-containedness."
  },
  "notes": {
    "why_this_track_exists": "The original held-out evaluation (outputs/phase2_holdout_eval/) used a manifest rebuilt from data/detector, which was later found to overlap substantially with data/yolo/train+valid at the underlying-photograph level (50.4% exact-ahash match, confirmed by visual inspection) because all four YOLO-family models were actually trained on data/yolo. This yolo-native-test track instead evaluates against data/yolo's own native test split, whose leakage against data/yolo/train+valid is much lower (2.95% exact ahash match; see supplementary/yolo_test_vs_yolo_train_ahash_check.csv in the research repo) though not exactly zero, which is disclosed rather than hidden.",
    "mAP_computed_from": "raw_predictions_conf0.001.json (full PR sweep via pycocotools COCOeval, 101-point interpolation, validated against toy perfect/zero-overlap sanity cases)",
    "per_class_PRF1_confusion_matrix_computed_from": "raw_predictions_conf0.50.json at the documented operating point (conf=0.50; NMS IoU=0.45 for YOLO26 models, RT-DETR is NMS-free/query-based with no iou= parameter applied), boxes matched to ground truth via greedy cross-class IoU>=0.50 matching (highest-confidence prediction claims best-IoU unclaimed ground truth first).",
    "model_class_index_remap": "This checkpoint's own best.pt/model.names ordering was independently re-verified against label_map.json (NOT assumed identical to another checkpoint's mapping); see environment_manifest.json's model_class_index_to_label_map_mapping for this checkpoint's exact table."
  }
